le\", \"Amazon\", \"AI investment\", \"LLM\"],\n    30→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    31→  },\n    32→  {\n    33→    \"title\": \"Claude Code quality postmortem reveals harness bugs\",\n    34→    \"description\": \"Anthropic published a postmortem explaining that recent Claude Code quality issues were caused by three separate bugs in the Claude Code harness, not the models themselves. One key bug caused older thinking to be cleared from idle sessions repeatedly, making Claude seem forgetful.\",\n    35→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    36→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    37→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/23/claude-code-quality/\",\n    38→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-23\",\n    39→    \"topics\": [\"Claude Code\", \"AI agents\", \"bugs\", \"Anthropic\", \"coding-agents\"],\n    40→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n    41→  },\n    42→  {\n    43→    \"title\": \"Qwen3.6-27B delivers flagship-level coding in 27B model\",\n    44→    \"description\": \"Qwen released Qwen3.6-27B, claiming flagship-level agentic coding performance that surpasses their previous 397B MoE model. The model is 55.6GB (vs 807GB for the previous) and performs well on local benchmarks including generating SVG images of pelicans on bicycles.\",\n    45→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    46→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    47→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/qwen3-6-27b/\",\n    48→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n    49→    \"topics\": [\"LLM\", \"open source\", \"coding\", \"local models\", \"Qwen\"],\n    50→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    51→  },\n    52→  {\n    53→    \"title\": \"Firefox 150 includes 271 vulnerability fixes from Claude Mythos Preview\",\n    54→    \"description\": \"Mozilla CTO Bobby Holley announced that Firefox 150 includes fixes for 271 vulnerabilities identified during evaluation with Claude Mythos Preview. He called it 'every bit as capable' as top security researchers and noted defenders finally have a chance to win decisively.\",\n    55→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Bobby Holley)\",\n    56→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    57→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/firefox-mythos/\",\n    58→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n    59→    \"topics\": [\"Claude\", \"Anthropic\", \"security\", \"Firefox\", \"AI safety\"],\n    60→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    61→  },\n    62→  {\n    63→    \"title\": \"GitHub Copilot changes pricing due to agentic compute demands\",\n    64→    \"description\": \"GitHub changed Copilot Individual plans, tightening usage limits and pausing signups. The announcement notes that agentic workflows have fundamentally changed compute demands, with long-running parallelized sessions consuming far more resources than the original plan structure supported.\",\n    65→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    66→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    67→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/github-copilot-pricing/\",\n    68→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n    69→    \"topics\": [\"GitHub Copilot\", \"pricing\", \"AI agents\", \"coding tools\"],\n    70→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n    71→  },\n    72→  {\n    73→    \"title\": \"Google says 75 percent of all its new code is AI-generated\",\n    74→    \"description\": \"Google CEO Sundar Pichai announced that 75% of all new code at Google is AI-generated, up from 50% last fall. Google created a 'strike team' to improve AI coding capabilities to catch up to Anthropic, which writes 70-90% of its code with Claude Code.\",\n    75→    \"author\": \"Stevie Bonifield\",\n    76→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    77→    \"url\": \"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/22/google-ai-generated-code\",\n    78→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n    79→    \"topics\": [\"Google\", \"AI coding\", \"Claude Code\", \"software development\"],\n    80→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    81→  },\n    82→  {\n    83→    \"title\": \"Anthropic's most dangerous AI model just fell into the wrong hands\",\n    84→    \"description\": \"Unauthorized group gained access to Anthropic's exclusive cyber tool Mythos. The breach is described as 'humiliating' and raises serious security concerns about powerful AI models being accessed outside authorized channels.\",\n    85→    \"author\": \"The Verge staff\",\n    86→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    87→    \"url\": \"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/22/anthropic-mythos-breach\",\n    88→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-22\",\n    89→    \"topics\": [\"Anthropic\", \"Claude Mythos\", \"security\", \"AI safety\", \"breach\"],\n    90→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    91→  },\n    92→  {\n    93→    \"title\": \"SpaceX cuts deal to possibly buy Cursor for $60 billion\",\n    94→    \"description\": \"SpaceX is working with Cursor and has an option to buy the AI coding startup for $60B. This shows the massive valuations and strategic importance being placed on AI coding tools.\",\n    95→    \"author\": \"Elizabeth Lopatto\",\n    96→    \"source\": \"TechMedia\",\n    97→    \"url\": \"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/21/spacex-cursor-acquisition\",\n    98→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-21\",\n    99→    \"topics\": [\"SpaceX\", \"Cursor\", \"AI coding\", \"acquisition\", \"startups\"],\n   100→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   101→  },\n   102→  {\n   103→    \"title\": \"Claude Token Counter adds model comparisons\",\n   104→    \"description\": \"Simon Willison upgraded his Claude Token Counter tool to compare token counts between models. Claude Opus 4.7 uses a new tokenizer that increases tokens by 1.0-1.35x compared to 4.6. For system prompts, he found a 1.46x increase, making Opus 4.7 roughly 40% more expensive despite identical pricing.\",\n   105→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   106→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   107→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/20/claude-token-counter/\",\n   108→    \"published_date\": \"2026-04-20\",\n   109→    \"topics\": [\"Claude\", \"to